-- title:
--   Monomial basis of the crossing ring W[x,y]/(xy-t)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $t \in W$. Consider the quotient ring `CrossingQuotient W t` $= W[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - t)$, that is, the polynomial ring in two variables indexed by `Fin 2` over $W$ modulo the ideal generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - C\,t$, and the family `monomial` $t : \mathbb{Z} \to W[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-t)$ which sends an integer $n$ to the class of $X_0^{n}$ when $n \ge 0$ and to the class of $X_1^{-n}$ when $n < 0$ (formally: the $n$-th power of the class of $X_0$ with exponent `n.toNat` if $0 \le n$, and the `(-n).toNat`-th power of the class of $X_1$ otherwise). The theorem asserts the conjunction of two statements: this $\mathbb{Z}$-indexed family is linearly independent over $W$, and the $W$-submodule spanned by its range is the whole of the quotient. Thus the classes $\dots, x_1^2, x_1, 1, x_0, x_0^2, \dots$ form a $W$-module basis of the crossing ring, although the conclusion is stated as the two separate properties rather than as a `Basis` structure.
--
--   This is the normal-form statement for the coordinate ring of a plane crossing $xy = t$ over an arbitrary base ring: every class is uniquely $f(x) + y\,g(y)$. It is used in the analysis of the crossing quotient (for instance to show that the images of the two coordinates are non-zero-divisors) and in the construction of the resolved model packages and charts for modular curves with nodal fibres.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_CrossingQuotient_linearIndependent_monomial_and_span_eq_top.lean

